{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויגר", :translit "va-yagar", :gloss "and he/it was afraid"} {:he "וירא שאול אשר הוא משכיל מאד ויגר מפניו", :translit "va-yira sha'ul asher hu maskil me'od va-yagar mipanav", :gloss "and Saul feared, that he was very discerning, and he was afraid of him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויגר" "ויגר"]}], :frame {:text "The Ba'al HaTurim notes a rare form of the verb ויגר ('and he was afraid'), which occurs only twice in Scripture. The other instance is in 1 Samuel 18:15, where Saul fears David because David's success is evident. By linking the two occurrences, he draws a parallel: just as Saul feared David because he saw David succeeding and acting wisely (1 Samuel 18:14–15), so Moab feared Israel upon seeing Israel's success.", :sources ["1 Samuel 18:14-15" "Numbers 22:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויגר מואב", :translit "va-yagar mo'av", :gloss "and Moab was afraid"} {:he "אילי מואב יאחזמו רעד", :translit "eilei mo'av ya'chazemum ra'ad", :gloss "the chiefs of Moab shall be seized with trembling"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Gezera shava: the root ג-ו-ר ('fear') in our verse links to the word רעד ('trembling') in Isaiah 15:4 about Moab."}], :frame {:text "Isaiah 15 is a prophetic oracle concerning Moab. Isaiah 15:4 states 'the chiefs of Moab shall be seized with trembling,' prophesying Moab's terror. The Ba'al HaTurim links the language of Moab's fear in Numbers 22:3 to Isaiah's prophecy, showing the prophetic verse as a direct echo of the narrative.", :sources ["Isaiah 15:4" "Numbers 22:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ויגר" "ויגר"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ויגר", :refs ["Genesis 20:1" "Genesis 21:34" "Numbers 22:3" "Deuteronomy 26:5" "1 Samuel 18:15" "Psalms 75:9"], :n 6, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ויגר", :refs ["Genesis 20:1" "Genesis 21:34" "Numbers 22:3" "Deuteronomy 26:5" "1 Samuel 18:15" "Psalms 75:9"], :n 6, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezera shava: the root ג-ו-ר ('fear') in our verse links to the word רעד ('trembling') in Isaiah 15:4 about Moab.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:39.579209527Z", :model "glm-5.2"}